1
00:00:03,303 --> 00:00:06,039
Why did you wait so long
before it got this bad?

2
00:00:06,306 --> 00:00:07,974
Why didn't you tell me?

3
00:00:08,908 --> 00:00:10,143
Hang in there!

4
00:00:10,276 --> 00:00:11,111
Dr. Jonouchi!

5
00:00:12,145 --> 00:00:13,713
Dr. Jonouchi!

6
00:00:13,913 --> 00:00:15,181
Call an ambulance!

7
00:00:36,469 --> 00:00:40,173
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

8
00:00:47,347 --> 00:00:50,216
The extra charge for this bed
seems expensive.

9
00:00:51,551 --> 00:00:53,720
This was the only vacant room,
so you'll have to deal with it.

10
00:00:55,822 --> 00:00:56,790
How do you feel?

11
00:00:57,891 --> 00:00:59,526
I'm guessing not great.

12
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:02,829
This bed is so comfortable!

13
00:01:02,929 --> 00:01:05,465
The private room is amazing.

14
00:01:05,598 --> 00:01:06,599
- Really?
- Yeah,

15
00:01:06,666 --> 00:01:09,402
come here. Lie down.

16
00:01:09,769 --> 00:01:10,837
- Really?
- Yes.

17
00:01:11,004 --> 00:01:13,006
Okay.

18
00:01:15,241 --> 00:01:16,709
You're right! It feels so nice.

19
00:01:25,952 --> 00:01:27,220
Let me do your surgery.

20
00:01:28,421 --> 00:01:29,789
I thought you would say that.

21
00:01:32,192 --> 00:01:33,126
But then,

22
00:01:34,994 --> 00:01:38,264
you know even for you,
this operation is too hard.

23
00:01:41,367 --> 00:01:44,504
Unresectable locally advanced
pancreatic cancer,

24
00:01:45,105 --> 00:01:46,439
stage 4A.

25
00:01:51,344 --> 00:01:55,882
The tumour has spread from
the pancreatic head to the body part,

26
00:01:56,216 --> 00:02:00,053
and even spread to celiac artery...
and to common hepatic artery.

27
00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:08,061
I'm all right.
I'm ready for this all right.

28
00:02:09,062 --> 00:02:11,698
The death rate of humans
is 100 percent, right?

29
00:02:12,298 --> 00:02:14,834
Sooner or later everyone dies.

30
00:02:15,568 --> 00:02:19,072
Moreover, I'm glad it was cancer,

31
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:21,574
Huh?

32
00:02:21,641 --> 00:02:24,377
Well... unlike other illnesses,

33
00:02:25,111 --> 00:02:28,414
you know exactly
how much time you have left.

34
00:02:30,850 --> 00:02:33,153
I want to make the best of
what is left of my time,

35
00:02:34,387 --> 00:02:37,223
and leave money for Mai.

36
00:02:40,527 --> 00:02:44,797
I plan to get plenty of money as
a down payment for my contract...

37
00:02:45,265 --> 00:02:46,466
with the Wang group
and then die.

38
00:02:51,204 --> 00:02:52,672
- Hey.
- Yes?

39
00:02:54,207 --> 00:02:56,042
Do you really plan to
go to the hospital in Shanghai?

40
00:03:02,382 --> 00:03:03,416
Yeah. So, please...

41
00:03:04,484 --> 00:03:07,987
help me so that they won't
find out about my illness.

42
00:03:10,290 --> 00:03:11,124
Hey.

43
00:03:12,125 --> 00:03:17,764
That's the only thing...
I can do for Mai.

44
00:03:23,603 --> 00:03:24,604
Now Director Hiruma

45
00:03:24,837 --> 00:03:28,508
will make the Director's round
with his staff physicians...

46
00:03:29,142 --> 00:03:30,376
<i>In 2016,</i>

47
00:03:30,610 --> 00:03:33,546
<i>the once sacrosanct university</i>
<i>medical system was in crisis.</i>

48
00:03:34,314 --> 00:03:36,482
<i>The system on which lives depend</i>

49
00:03:36,549 --> 00:03:38,518
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

50
00:03:39,018 --> 00:03:40,720
Look at what we are up to!

51
00:03:41,254 --> 00:03:43,423
- Hello.
- Hello.

52
00:03:43,489 --> 00:03:46,793
They are all celebrities from abroad
who have heard about the success

53
00:03:46,859 --> 00:03:51,364
of the simultaneous operation on a mother
and her baby, known as the Wang operation.

54
00:03:51,864 --> 00:03:53,399
- Hello.
- Hello.

55
00:03:53,466 --> 00:03:57,136
Toutei University hospital's
reputation is now soaring like unagi.

56
00:03:57,203 --> 00:03:59,205
It sounds old-fashioned though.

57
00:03:59,339 --> 00:04:01,741
You know unagi is eel in English.

58
00:04:02,108 --> 00:04:04,477
We emerge like an eel,
and let's hop and jump high.

59
00:04:04,811 --> 00:04:05,912
- Yes sir.
- Yes sir.

60
00:04:07,614 --> 00:04:09,749
Isn't he too optimistic about us?

61
00:04:10,383 --> 00:04:13,653
The Wang group has
already started scouting us...

62
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:15,722
Didn't they try to recruit you, too?

63
00:04:16,356 --> 00:04:17,924
Wait. You must be kidding.

64
00:04:18,891 --> 00:04:21,261
- Dr. Kitano isn't here.
- Hey.

65
00:04:21,427 --> 00:04:24,631
I heard that the world-famous
Kitano was the first one chosen.

66
00:04:24,697 --> 00:04:25,531
No way.

67
00:04:25,832 --> 00:04:27,867
Dr. Kaji... are you serious?

68
00:04:27,934 --> 00:04:28,801
Oh my!

69
00:04:28,935 --> 00:04:30,837
- Director!
- You scared me!

70
00:04:30,903 --> 00:04:32,772
Daimon! Get in the formation!

71
00:04:33,006 --> 00:04:33,973
I decline.

72
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:36,209
Part-timer, how about
getting in line just once!

73
00:04:36,342 --> 00:04:37,377
She is walking away.

74
00:04:37,443 --> 00:04:38,278
She is.

75
00:04:44,050 --> 00:04:45,718
DECIDED

76
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:49,022
UNDER NEGOTIATION
UNDER EXAMINATION

77
00:04:50,423 --> 00:04:52,392
UNDER NEGOTIATION

78
00:04:52,458 --> 00:04:53,593
At this rate,

79
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:58,965
all of our great doctors will be
taken away by Wang Group.

80
00:04:59,032 --> 00:05:00,867
NOT A THREAT

81
00:05:02,435 --> 00:05:03,269
Dummy.

82
00:05:04,170 --> 00:05:06,706
It's all your fault!

83
00:05:10,643 --> 00:05:11,577
Good morning.

84
00:05:12,845 --> 00:05:15,381
Huh? Where is the patient?

85
00:05:15,548 --> 00:05:16,416
She was discharged.

86
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:26,359
- Hello, Chao Wang.
- Hello.

87
00:05:27,026 --> 00:05:31,698
Dr. Jonouchi, are you going to join
Wang Group's new hospital, too?

88
00:05:32,465 --> 00:05:34,434
Yes, if their condition suits me.

89
00:05:34,634 --> 00:05:35,702
I see.

90
00:05:36,269 --> 00:05:39,972
I plan to start the New Year
in Shanghai.

91
00:05:40,106 --> 00:05:42,942
If I can,
I would like to go even sooner.

92
00:05:43,376 --> 00:05:46,045
I want to spend Christmas
in Shanghai with my daughter.

93
00:05:51,551 --> 00:05:55,254
If you hire me,
you definitely won't regret it.

94
00:06:03,963 --> 00:06:05,898
- Wow.
- Director,

95
00:06:05,965 --> 00:06:08,101
thanks to a referral by the Wang group,
now we have a new VIP patient,

96
00:06:08,167 --> 00:06:10,136
- the VIP of the VIPS!
- Who are they?

97
00:06:10,269 --> 00:06:12,171
A famous hotel franchise owner
and a candidate for the coming

98
00:06:12,305 --> 00:06:15,141
Presidential Election,
Leonardo Scope and his wife Diana.

99
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:16,743
For real? No way!

100
00:06:17,777 --> 00:06:20,913
If Mr. Scope's health issue is revealed,

101
00:06:20,980 --> 00:06:22,915
it could have an impact
on his political career.

102
00:06:23,282 --> 00:06:25,418
Therefore, he desires
to be treated here in secrecy.

103
00:06:25,685 --> 00:06:26,552
Oh, I see. I see.

104
00:06:26,619 --> 00:06:29,455
As the surgical chief,
I will be performing the operation.

105
00:06:29,589 --> 00:06:30,723
Nice to meet you.

106
00:06:31,090 --> 00:06:33,326
No, they have requested
Dr. Kitano to do it.

107
00:06:34,927 --> 00:06:36,662
What?

108
00:06:36,796 --> 00:06:38,865
Mrs. Scope desires to get
our state of the art anaesthesia...

109
00:06:39,065 --> 00:06:42,602
technique for a completely
painless delivery.

110
00:06:42,668 --> 00:06:44,537
Oh, that one?

111
00:06:52,245 --> 00:06:53,579
Should we do it?

112
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:57,750
- I have a pen
- I have a pen

113
00:06:58,084 --> 00:07:00,353
- I have an apple
- I have an apple

114
00:07:02,388 --> 00:07:04,123
- Apple pen!
- Apple pen!

115
00:07:09,595 --> 00:07:10,463
Oh, Yuitsumuni?

116
00:07:10,596 --> 00:07:11,764
How about we

117
00:07:11,831 --> 00:07:12,799
show them a live performance?

118
00:07:12,865 --> 00:07:14,667
That's a good idea!

119
00:07:14,734 --> 00:07:15,968
Rika, let's do this.

120
00:07:16,035 --> 00:07:16,903
Yes sir.

121
00:07:20,406 --> 00:07:23,810
- The one and only
- The one and only

122
00:07:24,010 --> 00:07:27,914
No other mountain
as high as us

123
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:32,718
The breeze follows and covers us

124
00:07:32,785 --> 00:07:36,088
- Let's keep walking our own way
- Let's keep walking our own way

125
00:07:36,222 --> 00:07:40,793
- Toutei! Toutei! Toutei! Toutei!
- Toutei! Toutei! Toutei! Toutei!

126
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:44,363
- Toutei is our pride
- Toutei is our pride

127
00:07:44,464 --> 00:07:48,434
- and it's the one and only
- and it's the one and only

128
00:07:49,068 --> 00:07:50,069
What did you think?

129
00:07:50,136 --> 00:07:51,704
That was hilarious!
I'm happy to hear that!

130
00:07:52,972 --> 00:07:55,508
- Great.
- Let's do it again.

131
00:07:55,575 --> 00:07:57,510
- Toutei!
- Toutei!

132
00:07:58,010 --> 00:08:01,113
I wonder if Jonouchi
will quit and leave after all.

133
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:04,884
Michiko, it doesn't seem like
anyone else is coming.

134
00:08:04,951 --> 00:08:06,152
Why don't we play as a threesome?

135
00:08:06,819 --> 00:08:07,854
No thanks.

136
00:08:13,893 --> 00:08:16,662
WHERE ARE YOU? MICHIKO IS
TERRIBLY WORRIED ABOUT YOU

137
00:08:18,297 --> 00:08:19,232
It's from Hiromi.

138
00:08:21,901 --> 00:08:22,869
Huh? What?

139
00:08:22,935 --> 00:08:27,974
"I'm in the middle of something,
so I won't play Mah-jong today."

140
00:08:28,474 --> 00:08:29,308
What is that?

141
00:08:29,909 --> 00:08:31,377
She has a horrible taste!

142
00:08:31,511 --> 00:08:33,379
I don't care anymore!

143
00:08:34,313 --> 00:08:36,649
Ouch!

144
00:08:36,782 --> 00:08:38,651
HIROMI JONUCHI
ANAESTHETIST

145
00:08:42,488 --> 00:08:45,791
Not noticing your charm until now...

146
00:08:46,325 --> 00:08:50,363
was a huge mistake on my part.

147
00:08:53,499 --> 00:08:56,636
I hate Japanese people who
flock together all the time.

148
00:08:56,769 --> 00:08:57,603
However,

149
00:08:59,505 --> 00:09:00,673
you're different.

150
00:09:01,541 --> 00:09:02,775
Frankly speaking,

151
00:09:03,075 --> 00:09:04,210
you are really...

152
00:09:05,077 --> 00:09:06,679
really my type.

153
00:09:09,582 --> 00:09:11,617
Let's go to Shanghai together.

154
00:09:15,922 --> 00:09:18,190
PRE-SURGERY CONFERENCE

155
00:09:18,858 --> 00:09:21,494
That's right. That's what he wants.

156
00:09:22,828 --> 00:09:23,996
Using an IRE knife...

157
00:09:24,063 --> 00:09:26,532
This week's pre-surgery
conference will now begin.

158
00:09:26,766 --> 00:09:29,068
Our first patient is Leonardo Scope.

159
00:09:29,135 --> 00:09:31,837
Male, 50 years old.
His nationality is American.

160
00:09:31,904 --> 00:09:34,874
He's diagnosed with locally advanced
pancreatic cancer?, stage 4A.

161
00:09:35,041 --> 00:09:37,009
Surgeon in charge, Dr. Kitano,
please take it from here.

162
00:09:40,012 --> 00:09:42,214
I will now announce the
team for this operation.

163
00:09:42,582 --> 00:09:44,984
- The first assistant...
- Here! Please let me do it.

164
00:09:45,084 --> 00:09:47,887
No, let me...

165
00:09:48,421 --> 00:09:50,957
The first assistant,
will be Dr. Daimon.

166
00:09:53,259 --> 00:09:54,393
I decline.

167
00:09:54,927 --> 00:09:55,828
Why not?

168
00:09:56,329 --> 00:09:59,465
Why are you turning down the
operation every surgeon here wants?

169
00:09:59,532 --> 00:10:00,366
Huh?

170
00:10:01,534 --> 00:10:02,568
I just don't feel like doing it.

171
00:10:03,469 --> 00:10:04,470
Fine.

172
00:10:05,504 --> 00:10:09,575
This time, we will be using an IRE knife.

173
00:10:12,945 --> 00:10:15,147
There are only few IRE knives in Japan.

174
00:10:15,548 --> 00:10:18,084
We can only use this for VIP patients.

175
00:10:18,951 --> 00:10:22,088
At a hospital in New York,
they used six electrodes...

176
00:10:22,154 --> 00:10:25,758
and destroyed cancer cells
with high-tension current.

177
00:10:33,899 --> 00:10:36,335
Okay. I will do it after all.

178
00:10:36,502 --> 00:10:37,570
Didn't you just refuse it?

179
00:10:37,903 --> 00:10:39,338
I changed my mind.

180
00:10:41,007 --> 00:10:44,910
Even you want to steal
my skill of the IRE knife.

181
00:10:45,544 --> 00:10:49,148
Okay.
Helpers with a desire are welcomed.

182
00:10:49,215 --> 00:10:51,984
- First assistant?
- No, third.

183
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:55,121
He's still stuck on her
refusal from earlier.

184
00:10:55,187 --> 00:10:57,056
Our super star is quite petty.

185
00:10:57,223 --> 00:11:00,059
Well, I'm sure Daimon
will refuse to be third assistant.

186
00:11:00,126 --> 00:11:03,896
Okay. I'm happy to be
the third assistant.

187
00:11:08,401 --> 00:11:10,269
Stop getting carried away!

188
00:11:11,237 --> 00:11:17,076
Most of the doctors in this room
have been scouted by Chinese money!

189
00:11:18,044 --> 00:11:19,378
I'm fed up with this!

190
00:11:19,945 --> 00:11:23,382
Isn't there anyone left here
with the Japanese spirit?

191
00:11:25,851 --> 00:11:26,852
Michiko Daimon,

192
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:29,722
I'm so disappointed at you.

193
00:11:30,456 --> 00:11:33,359
Third assistant?
Do you not have any pride left?

194
00:11:34,093 --> 00:11:35,428
This isn't right.

195
00:11:35,795 --> 00:11:37,596
Tell him you decline!

196
00:11:37,897 --> 00:11:39,031
I will do it.

197
00:11:40,566 --> 00:11:43,502
My hobby is surgery.

198
00:11:48,174 --> 00:11:50,042
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

199
00:11:50,743 --> 00:11:53,446
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>

200
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:55,514
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

201
00:11:56,182 --> 00:11:59,418
<i>Her solo weapons are her license and</i>

202
00:11:59,819 --> 00:12:01,053
<i>the skills she has earned.</i>

203
00:12:02,221 --> 00:12:04,457
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

204
00:12:04,957 --> 00:12:05,925
<i>Also known as</i>

205
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:08,060
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

206
00:12:37,757 --> 00:12:38,824
How are you feeling?

207
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:41,694
Please, stop talking about my illness.

208
00:12:41,761 --> 00:12:42,828
That's not what I mean.

209
00:12:43,262 --> 00:12:45,197
I'm asking if you also
have eye problems.

210
00:12:47,399 --> 00:12:48,501
You only like good-looking guys.

211
00:12:48,567 --> 00:12:49,902
What are you doing with Kitano?

212
00:12:51,470 --> 00:12:54,473
Maybe I like his amazing English.

213
00:12:56,108 --> 00:12:57,376
Okay, guys.

214
00:12:57,643 --> 00:12:59,478
All right then. Let's begin.

215
00:12:59,545 --> 00:13:01,747
We will now begin
irreversible electroporation...

216
00:13:01,881 --> 00:13:03,582
on Leonardo Scope...

217
00:13:03,749 --> 00:13:05,484
to dissolve his locally advanced
pancreatic cancer.

218
00:13:05,785 --> 00:13:08,020
His vitals are 130 and 73.

219
00:13:08,154 --> 00:13:09,255
Heart rate is 65.

220
00:13:09,688 --> 00:13:10,923
- Scalpel.
- Here you are.

221
00:13:12,258 --> 00:13:13,325
Incision.

222
00:13:18,197 --> 00:13:19,398
- Monopolar.
- Here you are.

223
00:13:24,503 --> 00:13:25,437
Kitano,

224
00:13:25,571 --> 00:13:28,507
I'm sure you're already know,
but there is no room for mistakes.

225
00:13:28,674 --> 00:13:32,111
They are operating on
the next presidential candidate.

226
00:13:35,114 --> 00:13:37,550
Are you trying to buy up
all the doctors?

227
00:13:38,551 --> 00:13:41,120
Are they like home appliances your
people are buying up from Japan?

228
00:13:49,428 --> 00:13:51,497
- IRE knife.
- Here you are.

229
00:14:00,139 --> 00:14:03,542
That is a super expensive IRE knife?

230
00:14:03,609 --> 00:14:06,278
- Connect the probe.
- Yes, sir.

231
00:14:13,118 --> 00:14:14,119
I got it.

232
00:14:14,753 --> 00:14:15,921
- One more time.
- Okay.

233
00:14:23,395 --> 00:14:26,332
Third assistant, stop looking around
and concentrate.

234
00:14:35,441 --> 00:14:37,576
It is in position.
Let's turn on the current.

235
00:14:37,877 --> 00:14:40,012
- Turn the voltage to 3000.
- Got it.

236
00:14:46,919 --> 00:14:49,288
Dr. Jonouchi, is the
muscular relaxation okay?

237
00:14:50,923 --> 00:14:52,524
The muscular relaxation is fine.

238
00:14:52,992 --> 00:14:55,694
- Heart rate is 72.
- Okay.

239
00:14:56,662 --> 00:14:57,730
Ablation.

240
00:14:59,999 --> 00:15:03,502
ABLATION, GALVANOCAUTERY

241
00:15:03,636 --> 00:15:05,437
IRE KNIFE, PAN CREASE, CANCER

242
00:15:19,151 --> 00:15:20,452
Complete.

243
00:15:21,453 --> 00:15:22,454
Perfect.

244
00:15:22,788 --> 00:15:23,622
Oh.

245
00:15:24,890 --> 00:15:25,891
Nice work.

246
00:15:26,091 --> 00:15:27,026
Nice work.

247
00:15:27,626 --> 00:15:28,861
Good work.

248
00:15:28,928 --> 00:15:30,229
Good work.

249
00:15:39,972 --> 00:15:41,106
Nice job.

250
00:15:41,206 --> 00:15:42,074
Nice work.

251
00:15:46,278 --> 00:15:47,212
Dr. Daimon.

252
00:15:49,715 --> 00:15:51,216
What is it exactly
you are trying to do?

253
00:15:51,784 --> 00:15:53,519
You volunteered
for third assistant...

254
00:15:53,652 --> 00:15:54,920
to steal the IRE knife, right?

255
00:15:54,987 --> 00:15:56,288
Please, let it slip.

256
00:15:56,422 --> 00:15:58,791
No way we can overlook you pick-pocketing
a hundred of thousand dollar knife.

257
00:15:58,857 --> 00:16:00,159
I'll give it back as soon
as I use it.

258
00:16:00,292 --> 00:16:02,628
Whose operation
do you plan to use that on?

259
00:16:07,266 --> 00:16:08,167
Huh?

260
00:16:08,734 --> 00:16:09,802
What is it?

261
00:16:10,769 --> 00:16:12,471
Are you serious?

262
00:16:33,892 --> 00:16:35,027
Let me operate on you.

263
00:16:36,729 --> 00:16:38,664
As long as I have this,
I can do the operation.

264
00:16:40,766 --> 00:16:41,967
This is nonsense.

265
00:16:42,735 --> 00:16:45,571
If the hospital finds that out,
you'll be fired and punished.

266
00:16:45,771 --> 00:16:47,806
You must stay alive...

267
00:16:48,474 --> 00:16:49,608
for Mai,

268
00:16:49,942 --> 00:16:52,444
Mr. Akira, and even me.

269
00:17:01,687 --> 00:17:04,623
- It's okay. I...
- I know.

270
00:17:08,961 --> 00:17:11,597
You don't need to say it.
I already know.

271
00:17:28,547 --> 00:17:29,448
I'm just...

272
00:17:32,184 --> 00:17:33,018
so scared.

273
00:17:36,688 --> 00:17:38,857
I know better than anyone...

274
00:17:42,728 --> 00:17:45,898
just how dangerous operation it is.

275
00:18:03,449 --> 00:18:04,283
Please.

276
00:18:08,253 --> 00:18:09,822
Please tell me...

277
00:18:12,357 --> 00:18:13,258
what you always say.

278
00:18:16,361 --> 00:18:17,629
Please...

279
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:20,699
Dr. Daimon.

280
00:18:33,612 --> 00:18:34,446
No need to worry.

281
00:18:36,215 --> 00:18:39,017
I never fail.

282
00:19:06,411 --> 00:19:08,747
Inject the right amount
of muscle relaxant.

283
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:10,549
I told you to leave it to me.

284
00:19:15,854 --> 00:19:17,556
What time do you think it is?

285
00:19:17,623 --> 00:19:18,724
You're not busy anyway.

286
00:19:21,293 --> 00:19:25,164
I am moved by your friendship
with Dr. Jonouchi.

287
00:19:27,366 --> 00:19:30,202
I won't tell anyone about you
breaking into the operating room...

288
00:19:30,269 --> 00:19:32,938
and even about stealing the knife.
Let's hurry before we're caught.

289
00:19:33,005 --> 00:19:35,073
Vitals are 126 and 61.

290
00:19:35,307 --> 00:19:36,775
Heart rate is 75.

291
00:19:37,342 --> 00:19:38,844
Scalpel. Thank you.

292
00:19:45,117 --> 00:19:45,951
Monopolar.

293
00:20:03,435 --> 00:20:06,171
Michiko. Relax.

294
00:20:14,680 --> 00:20:15,747
IRE knife.

295
00:20:17,916 --> 00:20:18,750
I'll pierce it into the tumour,
so hold it tight.

296
00:20:18,817 --> 00:20:20,152
- Got it.
- This way,

297
00:20:20,352 --> 00:20:22,721
we won't hurt her celiac artery.

298
00:20:29,328 --> 00:20:30,662
Do you really know
the location of each tumour...

299
00:20:30,729 --> 00:20:32,731
and blood vessel
without a navigation system?

300
00:20:32,998 --> 00:20:33,832
Okay.

301
00:20:35,167 --> 00:20:36,001
One more.

302
00:20:40,138 --> 00:20:41,773
She's very fast.

303
00:20:43,742 --> 00:20:44,576
Thanks.

304
00:20:46,612 --> 00:20:47,746
Let's turn on the power.

305
00:21:00,993 --> 00:21:02,294
One more time with

306
00:21:02,427 --> 00:21:03,762
a change of knife position.

307
00:21:08,567 --> 00:21:09,534
PVC!

308
00:21:09,668 --> 00:21:10,602
Her heart is contracting.

309
00:21:28,253 --> 00:21:29,454
Administer lidocaine.

310
00:21:30,322 --> 00:21:31,423
I will continue the current.

311
00:21:31,556 --> 00:21:32,391
Got it.

312
00:21:38,730 --> 00:21:39,931
Hold this.

313
00:21:40,732 --> 00:21:42,234
The PVC won't stop.

314
00:21:44,369 --> 00:21:47,339
If you continue, her heart will
not be able to take the current.

315
00:21:51,543 --> 00:21:52,611
This is dangerous.

316
00:21:56,181 --> 00:21:57,049
Dr. Daimon.

317
00:21:59,918 --> 00:22:03,088
Daimon, you never fail, right?

318
00:22:17,703 --> 00:22:20,439
This is as far as...

319
00:22:31,583 --> 00:22:32,451
Michiko.

320
00:22:35,420 --> 00:22:36,655
Close her up.

321
00:22:50,168 --> 00:22:51,036
Inoperable.

322
00:23:32,511 --> 00:23:35,547
The surgery is over.

323
00:23:38,583 --> 00:23:39,418
Yes.

324
00:23:45,957 --> 00:23:50,529
I've never seen that
kind of look on your face.

325
00:23:54,833 --> 00:23:56,067
I'm fine.

326
00:23:57,836 --> 00:23:59,438
Just tell me.

327
00:24:11,283 --> 00:24:15,320
I failed... to remove the entire tumour.

328
00:24:22,961 --> 00:24:24,463
I see.

329
00:24:31,803 --> 00:24:35,874
Just having the privilege of
being operated on...

330
00:24:38,643 --> 00:24:42,314
by a prominent Doctor Daimon
is enough for me.

331
00:24:54,960 --> 00:24:56,027
Daimon.

332
00:24:58,363 --> 00:25:01,233
Is it true that you stole the IRE knife?

333
00:25:01,500 --> 00:25:03,635
Furthermore, you used the
operating room without permission?

334
00:25:06,905 --> 00:25:07,772
Come with me.

335
00:25:28,760 --> 00:25:32,297
It's my fault.

336
00:25:34,766 --> 00:25:36,701
You do have guts.

337
00:25:36,768 --> 00:25:38,537
Why don't we report to the police?

338
00:25:38,603 --> 00:25:40,572
I'm sure she will do that again.

339
00:25:41,172 --> 00:25:44,476
Dr. Daimon, you did that...

340
00:25:45,110 --> 00:25:48,580
to save your fellow doctor, right?

341
00:25:48,847 --> 00:25:52,851
Kikawada, you know I can never...

342
00:25:53,318 --> 00:25:57,656
send such a great doctor...
off to the police.

343
00:25:57,756 --> 00:26:00,158
- Are you saying I'm not punished?
- That's right.

344
00:26:01,126 --> 00:26:02,861
I feel like you have an ulterior motive.

345
00:26:02,961 --> 00:26:07,966
I think outstanding individuals like you
should belong to an organisation.

346
00:26:08,133 --> 00:26:11,469
- Why don't you work for my...
- I decline.

347
00:26:11,536 --> 00:26:13,204
That was fast.

348
00:26:13,371 --> 00:26:15,507
The director is still talking.

349
00:26:15,707 --> 00:26:17,576
Director, get to the point.

350
00:26:18,009 --> 00:26:21,713
Oh, right. Dr. Daimon,

351
00:26:22,581 --> 00:26:26,251
we've been flooded with requests
to get operation by you.

352
00:26:26,985 --> 00:26:29,921
They all are celebrities who came
here by Mr. Wang's recommendation.

353
00:26:30,221 --> 00:26:34,192
As your penalty this time, we will have
you perform all of these operations.

354
00:26:35,794 --> 00:26:36,828
Yes sir.

355
00:26:37,696 --> 00:26:42,100
I want you to take on those operations
at free of charge.

356
00:26:42,167 --> 00:26:44,169
This is a penalty after all.

357
00:26:44,469 --> 00:26:45,937
I have conditions as well.

358
00:26:46,237 --> 00:26:47,105
What is that?

359
00:26:47,238 --> 00:26:50,508
Let Dr. Jonouchi stay in
the suite for the rest of the year.

360
00:26:51,343 --> 00:26:52,377
I guess I can do that.

361
00:26:52,644 --> 00:26:53,478
Furthermore, for free.

362
00:26:55,680 --> 00:26:58,650
Mr. Wang has said
that he desires to...

363
00:27:00,986 --> 00:27:02,787
revoke the contract
between you and him.

364
00:27:06,257 --> 00:27:07,525
I understand.

365
00:27:08,960 --> 00:27:13,098
Why didn't you tell... about your illness?

366
00:27:18,470 --> 00:27:22,173
I'm a little shocked
to find out you asked Daimon

367
00:27:24,409 --> 00:27:26,277
to perform your operation.

368
00:27:27,445 --> 00:27:31,249
Why wasn't it me... but her?

369
00:27:32,784 --> 00:27:33,985
That's because...

370
00:27:34,886 --> 00:27:35,854
Because...

371
00:27:38,323 --> 00:27:41,993
Dr. Daimon is more skilled... than you.

372
00:27:44,095 --> 00:27:48,033
Thank you for worrying about me.
I wish you happiness with your wife.

373
00:28:11,823 --> 00:28:15,560
I will... never give up.

374
00:28:23,435 --> 00:28:26,604
Dr. Daimon, welcome.

375
00:28:26,805 --> 00:28:28,073
- Hello.
- Hello.

376
00:28:30,942 --> 00:28:32,310
I'll go to Shanghai.

377
00:28:32,777 --> 00:28:36,347
But in exchange, I want you to
prepare the down payment in cash.

378
00:28:38,516 --> 00:28:39,784
That's fine.

379
00:28:40,618 --> 00:28:42,487
I'll gladly pay you
as much as you want.

380
00:28:42,687 --> 00:28:44,089
He said that is fine.

381
00:28:45,490 --> 00:28:46,591
Is our deal made, then?

382
00:28:47,325 --> 00:28:48,159
Hello.

383
00:28:48,727 --> 00:28:49,561
Goodbye.

384
00:28:50,462 --> 00:28:51,463
How much do you want?

385
00:28:51,596 --> 00:28:52,797
How much do you want?

386
00:28:57,402 --> 00:28:59,471
Please tell us the exact amount you want.

387
00:29:03,341 --> 00:29:04,175
This much.

388
00:29:10,615 --> 00:29:12,350
Is 30,000 dollars too much?

389
00:29:13,818 --> 00:29:17,222
300 MILLION DOLLARS IS TOO MUCH

390
00:29:18,990 --> 00:29:21,292
Are you going to pay or not?

391
00:29:25,964 --> 00:29:27,799
Okay.

392
00:29:30,502 --> 00:29:31,336
Oh! Thank you!

393
00:29:32,403 --> 00:29:34,839
Let's take this back to
the drawing board.

394
00:29:36,007 --> 00:29:38,409
What?

395
00:29:39,244 --> 00:29:40,779
You're pretty stingy.

396
00:29:41,479 --> 00:29:43,681
Then, 10,000 dollars will be fine.

397
00:29:43,748 --> 00:29:44,616
Even 5,000.

398
00:29:44,682 --> 00:29:45,650
What is she saying?

399
00:29:45,717 --> 00:29:46,651
What does she mean?

400
00:29:46,718 --> 00:29:47,886
I need money!

401
00:29:47,952 --> 00:29:49,788
Get her out of here!

402
00:29:49,854 --> 00:29:51,256
See you again.

403
00:29:56,528 --> 00:29:57,862
Wait! My bag! My bag! My bag!

404
00:29:59,097 --> 00:29:59,998
Hey, wait.

405
00:30:00,098 --> 00:30:03,668
Gosh! How stingy.

406
00:30:04,769 --> 00:30:05,637
Wait.

407
00:30:06,838 --> 00:30:07,939
Oh my.

408
00:30:09,174 --> 00:30:12,243
You better not do this. He is stingy.

409
00:30:13,278 --> 00:30:14,112
Daimon.

410
00:30:16,347 --> 00:30:17,649
There was a misunderstanding of
adding two more zeros...

411
00:30:18,116 --> 00:30:19,484
Letters of resignation.

412
00:30:19,784 --> 00:30:24,823
All of these doctors have been
headhunted by Wang's hospital.

413
00:30:25,523 --> 00:30:27,859
Haven't you really noticed
nothing until now?

414
00:30:27,926 --> 00:30:29,894
This is ridiculous.

415
00:30:30,094 --> 00:30:32,463
Aren't you two leaving too?

416
00:30:32,530 --> 00:30:34,098
- No way.
- That's absurd.

417
00:30:37,869 --> 00:30:41,706
I am not going to approve of this!

418
00:30:41,773 --> 00:30:42,607
Pardon?

419
00:30:43,041 --> 00:30:50,014
If there is going to be anyone
who resigns for real,

420
00:30:50,815 --> 00:30:52,984
you're both fired.

421
00:30:54,619 --> 00:30:55,787
Well, that is...

422
00:30:55,854 --> 00:30:56,888
- Yes sir.
- Yes sir.

423
00:30:56,955 --> 00:30:58,690
It's too late.

424
00:30:59,524 --> 00:31:01,893
It's no use crying over spilt milk.

425
00:31:10,835 --> 00:31:13,271
It wasn't long, but
thank you for having me.

426
00:31:13,504 --> 00:31:15,073
Kitano! You too?

427
00:31:15,406 --> 00:31:19,477
Kitano. please give up on your plan.

428
00:31:19,544 --> 00:31:20,411
Kitano.

429
00:31:21,379 --> 00:31:27,352
If you are to leave this hospital
right now, we will be in big trouble.

430
00:31:30,388 --> 00:31:33,291
Please, reconsider it.

431
00:31:34,592 --> 00:31:36,928
If you do, I'll do anything you want.

432
00:31:37,528 --> 00:31:39,631
Look how far the director
is going for you!

433
00:31:40,565 --> 00:31:44,569
Kitano. I'll do anything.

434
00:31:45,403 --> 00:31:46,671
Kitano.

435
00:31:46,738 --> 00:31:49,073
- Kitano! Please!
- Please.

436
00:31:55,546 --> 00:31:57,615
Please don't do this.

437
00:31:57,682 --> 00:31:59,384
- Please.
- Please.

438
00:32:00,385 --> 00:32:02,654
My answer... is no.

439
00:32:03,888 --> 00:32:05,189
Kitano, you must be kidding.

440
00:32:06,190 --> 00:32:10,028
Who do you think made you
who you are?

441
00:32:10,695 --> 00:32:12,130
When I worked in the medical office,

442
00:32:12,430 --> 00:32:14,933
you professors treated
me like dirt.

443
00:32:15,400 --> 00:32:16,834
You neither let me handle a scalpel

444
00:32:16,968 --> 00:32:18,970
nor let me assist any operation.

445
00:32:19,037 --> 00:32:23,174
Do you still dwell on it?

446
00:32:23,374 --> 00:32:27,345
I wanted to bring you to your knees
with my new medical skills.

447
00:32:27,478 --> 00:32:29,380
So we're on our knees now.

448
00:32:29,514 --> 00:32:34,185
However, I realised that you're
too unskilled to compete,

449
00:32:34,385 --> 00:32:37,155
so there's no point in winning.

450
00:32:37,956 --> 00:32:39,724
The reason for me to stay here is...

451
00:32:40,391 --> 00:32:41,893
none whatsoever.

452
00:32:42,961 --> 00:32:47,265
- Kitano!
- Kitano!

453
00:32:50,868 --> 00:32:51,803
My dear brother,

454
00:32:52,470 --> 00:32:54,906
this hospital is so corrupt.

455
00:32:56,274 --> 00:32:57,642
It is impossible to clean it.

456
00:33:00,411 --> 00:33:01,279
It's good.

457
00:33:03,181 --> 00:33:06,718
Are you trying to scare me to death?

458
00:33:07,018 --> 00:33:08,720
How creepy.

459
00:33:14,292 --> 00:33:15,126
Deputy Director.

460
00:33:15,893 --> 00:33:16,761
What?

461
00:33:17,729 --> 00:33:19,497
Let's unite together.

462
00:33:19,864 --> 00:33:20,898
Huh?

463
00:33:20,965 --> 00:33:24,402
Do I have to go through
this test every day?

464
00:33:24,469 --> 00:33:25,303
Yes.

465
00:33:27,372 --> 00:33:30,308
Oh, Mai is coming home
for Christmas, right?

466
00:33:30,575 --> 00:33:31,542
You must be excited.

467
00:33:32,043 --> 00:33:32,944
I am.

468
00:33:39,884 --> 00:33:43,021
God is really unkind, isn't he?

469
00:33:43,588 --> 00:33:46,591
How can he treat
a single mother like this?

470
00:33:56,667 --> 00:33:59,771
I wonder how much time I have left.

471
00:34:01,939 --> 00:34:04,876
If I estimate,
it might be about three months.

472
00:34:05,877 --> 00:34:07,045
There is no such thing as
an estimate of remaining life.

473
00:34:07,311 --> 00:34:10,114
It's just an excuse for doctors
to dodge responsibility.

474
00:34:18,689 --> 00:34:19,524
Hey,

475
00:34:20,758 --> 00:34:22,493
isn't there a man you'd like to see?

476
00:34:23,127 --> 00:34:24,028
Huh?

477
00:34:25,930 --> 00:34:29,233
- Unfortunately, no.
- What?

478
00:34:32,136 --> 00:34:33,938
After I realised I was sick,

479
00:34:34,906 --> 00:34:38,209
I couldn't help but worry about
Mai after my death.

480
00:34:39,577 --> 00:34:42,180
I kept thinking that I have to
leave money behind for Mai.

481
00:34:43,915 --> 00:34:46,751
But it's not really about money.

482
00:34:47,752 --> 00:34:48,953
What I want the most...

483
00:34:51,322 --> 00:34:52,490
is staying alive.

484
00:34:55,493 --> 00:34:57,862
I want to see Mai become
a prima donna.

485
00:34:58,629 --> 00:35:00,264
Yeah.

486
00:35:01,332 --> 00:35:03,401
And if she fails,

487
00:35:04,936 --> 00:35:05,770
I want to cry with her.

488
00:35:07,839 --> 00:35:09,240
I want to fall in love...

489
00:35:10,241 --> 00:35:13,244
and marry a great man again!

490
00:35:14,545 --> 00:35:18,916
And just once, I want to win a round
of Mah-jong with 30,000 points.

491
00:35:18,983 --> 00:35:20,785
- That's...
- Do you get it?

492
00:35:21,385 --> 00:35:27,358
Also, I want to wear a short skirt...
and expose my bear legs like you.

493
00:35:27,425 --> 00:35:28,359
You're kidding.

494
00:35:30,094 --> 00:35:31,863
- Also,
- There's more?

495
00:35:32,864 --> 00:35:34,499
You're quite greedy.

496
00:35:36,200 --> 00:35:37,535
I want to operate more.

497
00:35:39,437 --> 00:35:41,806
Even now I still get nervous
during surgery,

498
00:35:42,807 --> 00:35:45,076
and there are times I get scared
and want to run.

499
00:35:47,445 --> 00:35:48,279
However,

500
00:35:49,647 --> 00:35:52,150
when I listen to the heart beats
of patients,

501
00:35:54,185 --> 00:35:56,053
I feel like I am alive as well.

502
00:35:58,022 --> 00:36:03,327
I feel like I'm living a very crucial
moment with the patient.

503
00:36:07,532 --> 00:36:09,734
I'm sure you also know how it feels.

504
00:36:13,838 --> 00:36:18,776
I want to perform important
operations with you, Dr. Daimon.

505
00:36:55,379 --> 00:36:56,681
Even though you didn't fail,

506
00:36:58,249 --> 00:37:01,652
every doctor has experienced

507
00:37:04,622 --> 00:37:06,857
a sense of defeat, feeling hopeless.

508
00:37:09,660 --> 00:37:11,562
There are things beyond
human reach, you know.

509
00:37:43,461 --> 00:37:45,630
Thank you for allowing
me to stay out overnight.

510
00:37:45,997 --> 00:37:46,931
You must be careful.

511
00:37:47,732 --> 00:37:48,633
Oh, they're here!

512
00:37:48,766 --> 00:37:51,102
Mai has arrived safely!

513
00:37:51,168 --> 00:37:52,503
Mum, I'm home!

514
00:37:52,570 --> 00:37:54,272
- Take off your shoes!
- She's back.

515
00:37:54,338 --> 00:37:55,206
Welcome home.

516
00:38:03,714 --> 00:38:07,852
Mr. Akira splurged on special meat today,

517
00:38:07,918 --> 00:38:09,186
so eat up!

518
00:38:09,253 --> 00:38:11,689
Thank you. Let's eat!

519
00:38:15,059 --> 00:38:16,060
Enjoy.

520
00:38:16,127 --> 00:38:18,663
Mai, do you remember this?

521
00:38:18,963 --> 00:38:20,398
Yes, the ferocious shark!

522
00:38:21,065 --> 00:38:23,334
- Right.
- When I worked on holiday,

523
00:38:23,401 --> 00:38:25,903
- Mr. Akira babysat you.
- Yes.

524
00:38:26,270 --> 00:38:28,039
When we came home after the operation,

525
00:38:28,105 --> 00:38:30,775
Mr. Akira was completely exhausted.

526
00:38:30,841 --> 00:38:33,177
Premium meat!

527
00:38:34,679 --> 00:38:37,648
I'm going to eat you!

528
00:38:37,882 --> 00:38:39,517
One more time!

529
00:38:39,717 --> 00:38:43,387
Looking at you grow up so much,

530
00:38:43,454 --> 00:38:45,589
the ferocious shark is much impressed.

531
00:38:45,656 --> 00:38:48,125
Don't take my beef rib.

532
00:38:49,193 --> 00:38:54,031
It's fine because she's on vacation.
You have to take loads of nutrients!

533
00:38:57,468 --> 00:38:58,803
You're not going to eat, Mum?

534
00:39:02,006 --> 00:39:03,607
No, I'm not really hungry.

535
00:39:03,874 --> 00:39:05,776
- Are you on a diet?
- No.

536
00:39:09,547 --> 00:39:10,414
Mai,

537
00:39:12,116 --> 00:39:12,950
well...

538
00:39:14,752 --> 00:39:16,554
I have something important
to talk to you about.

539
00:39:16,987 --> 00:39:17,955
What is it?

540
00:39:21,625 --> 00:39:24,528
To tell the truth, I...

541
00:39:24,595 --> 00:39:25,730
Let me guess.

542
00:39:26,297 --> 00:39:28,099
Do you have a boyfriend?

543
00:39:28,265 --> 00:39:29,600
Are you getting remarried?

544
00:39:31,402 --> 00:39:33,104
No, no.

545
00:39:35,339 --> 00:39:36,941
It's about something else.

546
00:39:42,012 --> 00:39:44,648
For now, let's eat!

547
00:39:45,316 --> 00:39:46,751
Yeah, let's dig in.

548
00:39:47,585 --> 00:39:48,419
Let's eat.

549
00:39:48,486 --> 00:39:52,623
Barbecue on Christmas is the best!

550
00:39:56,994 --> 00:39:59,230
I'll have a bite as well.

551
00:40:03,167 --> 00:40:04,268
It's delicious.

552
00:40:04,468 --> 00:40:05,603
Don't push yourself.

553
00:40:06,871 --> 00:40:11,075
I don't. It really... is delicious.

554
00:40:18,983 --> 00:40:19,950
Let's go to the hospital.

555
00:40:20,418 --> 00:40:21,285
Huh?

556
00:40:21,352 --> 00:40:22,186
The hospital?

557
00:40:22,286 --> 00:40:23,154
Why?

558
00:40:23,687 --> 00:40:25,423
There is so much meat leftover.

559
00:40:25,489 --> 00:40:26,390
Anyhow, let's go.

560
00:40:28,492 --> 00:40:30,428
Mr. Akira and Mai,
please take your time.

561
00:40:31,328 --> 00:40:32,630
- Wait, Michiko.
- What's going on?

562
00:40:43,641 --> 00:40:44,675
Yes!

563
00:40:46,744 --> 00:40:48,312
Your cancer has gone down a stage.

564
00:40:48,979 --> 00:40:52,483
What do you mean? Didn't you say
you couldn't remove all the tumours?

565
00:40:52,683 --> 00:40:55,619
If the cells are removed as much
as possible with an IRE knife,

566
00:40:55,753 --> 00:40:57,455
it's possible to downgrade the stage,

567
00:40:57,521 --> 00:40:58,556
and I bet on it.

568
00:40:59,890 --> 00:41:01,659
The size of the tumours has shrunk,

569
00:41:01,725 --> 00:41:03,694
and it doesn't seem to infiltrate
into the blood vessels.

570
00:41:06,096 --> 00:41:06,931
That means...

571
00:41:07,131 --> 00:41:10,000
If we operate right away,
you can make a complete recovery.

572
00:41:17,041 --> 00:41:20,911
God isn't as unkind as you thought!

573
00:41:26,650 --> 00:41:28,319
You're quitting too?

574
00:41:29,954 --> 00:41:31,622
Diana has gone into labour.

575
00:41:31,755 --> 00:41:33,557
- Use the operating room.
- Okay.

576
00:41:35,292 --> 00:41:36,494
Let me use an operating room.

577
00:41:36,560 --> 00:41:39,263
- Oh no. It's just gone out.
- Please.

578
00:41:39,363 --> 00:41:41,298
- Sorry, it's not possible.
- Please.

579
00:41:41,432 --> 00:41:44,235
Mrs. Scope is our priority.
It's not possible.

580
00:41:45,202 --> 00:41:47,171
What country are we in?

581
00:41:47,505 --> 00:41:48,639
Japan, why?

582
00:41:48,839 --> 00:41:50,641
Japanese pay tax,

583
00:41:51,075 --> 00:41:53,310
and they can't even use
the national university's hospital?

584
00:41:53,878 --> 00:41:58,015
Filling this hospital with rich
foreigners are absolutely absurd.

585
00:41:58,649 --> 00:42:01,385
You never know what a hard work
it is to be the top director.

586
00:42:02,152 --> 00:42:02,987
So, keep your mouth shut!

587
00:42:04,154 --> 00:42:05,823
Go ahead and get ready for surgery.

588
00:42:20,671 --> 00:42:22,273
Childbirth is not an illness!

589
00:42:22,806 --> 00:42:24,942
You can do it on your own!

590
00:42:26,577 --> 00:42:27,745
- To the delivery room.
- Got it.

591
00:42:30,548 --> 00:42:35,853
I'm telling you I, as a qualified Japanese
midwife, will take care of you!

592
00:42:35,920 --> 00:42:36,887
Understand?

593
00:42:49,633 --> 00:42:51,235
Pull yourself together!

594
00:43:02,079 --> 00:43:03,180
Thanks, old lady.

595
00:43:03,247 --> 00:43:05,783
OPERATING ROOM

596
00:43:11,989 --> 00:43:13,157
You're the only one here?

597
00:43:13,891 --> 00:43:15,359
Well, it's Christmas.

598
00:43:23,367 --> 00:43:25,703
I cancelled my date
at the last minute.

599
00:43:25,803 --> 00:43:26,937
She's so angry!

600
00:43:27,237 --> 00:43:29,173
Wang is the one who is angry,
Dr. Kaji.

601
00:43:29,239 --> 00:43:32,209
I just stood him up for his
tens of million dollar contract.

602
00:43:34,678 --> 00:43:35,579
Thanks.

603
00:43:40,818 --> 00:43:44,455
I wonder what Mum wanted to talk about.

604
00:43:45,089 --> 00:43:47,257
- Let's go pray.
- Okay.

605
00:43:49,693 --> 00:43:55,099
- Silent night
- Silent night

606
00:43:55,766 --> 00:44:01,271
- Holy night
- Holy night

607
00:44:02,806 --> 00:44:03,641
Mai.

608
00:44:05,442 --> 00:44:08,946
Your Mum... is sick.

609
00:44:10,481 --> 00:44:11,915
What's wrong with her?

610
00:44:12,883 --> 00:44:15,386
She has something called
pancreatic cancer.

611
00:44:16,720 --> 00:44:17,855
It's pretty serious.

612
00:44:20,090 --> 00:44:22,693
But... she'll be fine.

613
00:44:24,128 --> 00:44:26,697
Michiko Daimon will take care of her.

614
00:44:29,299 --> 00:44:31,268
We will now begin the removal
of Hiromi Jonouchi's...

615
00:44:31,402 --> 00:44:34,204
reduced tumour
in the pancreas-duodenum.

616
00:44:35,272 --> 00:44:36,106
- Scalpel.
- Here you are.

617
00:44:36,240 --> 00:44:37,708
Hey, what do you think you're doing?

618
00:44:38,008 --> 00:44:40,044
Daimon, this time you're fired!

619
00:44:40,210 --> 00:44:42,179
Kaji! Hara!

620
00:44:42,246 --> 00:44:44,181
- We can hear you.
- You're fired, too!

621
00:44:44,415 --> 00:44:45,416
Well...

622
00:44:47,084 --> 00:44:49,920
I'm just a part-timer anyway.

623
00:44:50,754 --> 00:44:53,190
We're just a part-timer's assistants.

624
00:45:09,506 --> 00:45:10,441
Daimon.

625
00:45:11,408 --> 00:45:13,410
That's not Mrs. Scope's operation.

626
00:45:15,512 --> 00:45:16,346
Hey!

627
00:45:21,885 --> 00:45:24,254
I'll ligate the
pancreas-duodenum's artery.

628
00:45:24,321 --> 00:45:25,322
- 30 silk.
- Here you are.

629
00:45:33,630 --> 00:45:34,698
- Clipper.
- Here you are.

630
00:45:38,102 --> 00:45:39,203
- One more.
- Here you are.

631
00:45:47,211 --> 00:45:48,312
Dr. Daimon,

632
00:45:48,512 --> 00:45:50,047
- she's haemorrhaging.
- Why?

633
00:45:50,247 --> 00:45:53,484
That's because the artery
has been cut by the IRE knife.

634
00:45:53,550 --> 00:45:55,586
- Let's stanch bleeding. Gauze.
- Here you are.

635
00:45:56,053 --> 00:45:58,655
This is bad. There could be
damage to the portal vein.

636
00:45:58,822 --> 00:46:01,325
Her blood pressure is falling.
It's in the 60's! Heart rate is 100!

637
00:46:01,391 --> 00:46:04,027
- Suction! Prepare for a transfusion!
- Got it!

638
00:46:07,731 --> 00:46:08,932
The bleeding won't stop!

639
00:46:21,211 --> 00:46:22,045
Dr. Kitano.

640
00:46:23,614 --> 00:46:24,515
Kitano.

641
00:46:24,681 --> 00:46:26,383
What do you think you're doing?

642
00:46:27,317 --> 00:46:28,385
Hey, Kitano!

643
00:46:31,188 --> 00:46:33,824
Retract the gut and check the vein.

644
00:46:33,891 --> 00:46:35,592
Remove the head of
the pancreas and lift it up.

645
00:46:35,659 --> 00:46:36,493
Okay.

646
00:46:40,631 --> 00:46:42,599
- I'll operate the head part.
- Thank you.

647
00:46:43,534 --> 00:46:45,435
- Gauze.
- Here you are.

648
00:46:50,507 --> 00:46:51,742
I see.

649
00:46:52,709 --> 00:46:55,479
With that, the bleeding of the
portal vein can be controlled.

650
00:46:59,049 --> 00:46:59,883
Director.

651
00:47:01,485 --> 00:47:02,319
Have a seat.

652
00:47:06,190 --> 00:47:08,425
Again? Daimon...

653
00:47:17,201 --> 00:47:19,436
Haemorrhage of the portal vein
has been confirmed.

654
00:47:20,370 --> 00:47:21,638
Suture...

655
00:47:21,705 --> 00:47:23,407
- with 60 polypropylene.
- Here you are.

656
00:47:37,120 --> 00:47:38,655
Please save my mum.

657
00:47:41,491 --> 00:47:42,392
Please!

658
00:47:55,272 --> 00:47:59,109
It's okay, Mai. I won't give up.

659
00:48:09,019 --> 00:48:14,958
Lord, please help... Daimon.

660
00:48:22,866 --> 00:48:26,103
I never fail.

661
00:48:42,452 --> 00:48:46,123
A healthy baby boy!
He looks just like you.

662
00:48:57,634 --> 00:48:59,136
Gastrojejunostomy is complete.

663
00:48:59,202 --> 00:49:00,837
Let's control the bleeding.

664
00:49:01,071 --> 00:49:02,239
- Monopolar.
- Here you are.

665
00:49:05,642 --> 00:49:07,744
- Please wipe Dr. Daimon's face.
- Got it.

666
00:49:09,246 --> 00:49:10,080
Excuse me.

667
00:49:53,824 --> 00:49:55,392
You did well, Michiko.

668
00:49:55,459 --> 00:49:57,160
Daimon, great job.

669
00:49:57,294 --> 00:49:59,496
Good job, Dr. Daimon.

670
00:49:59,763 --> 00:50:00,964
Perfect.

671
00:50:02,833 --> 00:50:05,869
Thanks to all of you,
we could succeed.

672
00:50:07,704 --> 00:50:08,905
Merry Christmas.

673
00:50:10,207 --> 00:50:11,808
- Merry Christmas.
- Merry Christmas.

674
00:50:12,342 --> 00:50:15,345
- Merry Christmas.
- Merry Christmas.

675
00:50:15,812 --> 00:50:17,247
Merry Christmas.

676
00:50:21,385 --> 00:50:22,219
Doctors,

677
00:50:23,487 --> 00:50:27,124
I also wish you a merry Christmas.

678
00:50:29,326 --> 00:50:31,061
Thank you, miracle.

679
00:50:50,514 --> 00:50:51,882
Happy New Year.

680
00:50:52,149 --> 00:50:53,717
Happy New Year.

681
00:50:54,151 --> 00:50:56,086
Chao Wang clinic

682
00:50:56,887 --> 00:50:59,556
has employed the best doctors,

683
00:51:00,323 --> 00:51:01,324
and today is...

684
00:51:01,725 --> 00:51:03,060
our opening celebration.

685
00:51:05,328 --> 00:51:10,734
Now the world-known
Dr. Kitano will deliver a speech.

686
00:51:19,176 --> 00:51:21,945
There are no borders
in the field of medicine.

687
00:51:22,546 --> 00:51:27,117
Even in new areas,
we must aim for the top.

688
00:51:32,622 --> 00:51:35,058
Wipe the glass more!

689
00:51:37,094 --> 00:51:38,895
Deputy Director, what are you doing?

690
00:51:38,962 --> 00:51:42,032
Not deputy, I'm Director Toko Kubo.

691
00:51:42,099 --> 00:51:43,667
- Hello.
- Hello.

692
00:51:43,733 --> 00:51:44,868
Nice to see you.

693
00:51:50,874 --> 00:51:54,077
This hospital needs thorough cleaning!

694
00:51:55,011 --> 00:52:00,117
I will teach you the spirit
of the Japanese.

695
00:52:02,319 --> 00:52:04,321
Say, "Yes ma'am"!

696
00:52:05,355 --> 00:52:06,690
- Yes ma'am.
- Yes ma'am.

697
00:52:08,959 --> 00:52:09,860
Oh my god.

698
00:52:13,897 --> 00:52:17,300
Everyone, happy new year.

699
00:52:17,667 --> 00:52:19,269
- Happy new year.
- Happy new year.

700
00:52:20,303 --> 00:52:24,808
Oh, right. Why don't you move up
and get together at the front?

701
00:52:27,477 --> 00:52:29,012
Not many are left.

702
00:52:29,479 --> 00:52:30,480
Do you need to say it?

703
00:52:31,047 --> 00:52:33,750
I should be in Shanghai too.

704
00:52:34,451 --> 00:52:36,953
What are you laughing at?
You didn't even get the offer.

705
00:52:37,387 --> 00:52:39,823
Toutei University hospital...

706
00:52:39,956 --> 00:52:44,261
will undertake the reform for the
first time since its establishment.

707
00:52:44,628 --> 00:52:51,034
The internal medicine and the surgery
departments have been divided so far.

708
00:52:51,101 --> 00:52:56,640
But from now on, we will merge
them as one and work together.

709
00:52:56,706 --> 00:52:58,008
- Director,
- From now on...

710
00:52:58,608 --> 00:53:01,411
Thank you for
the moving final speech.

711
00:53:01,478 --> 00:53:03,113
I'm not finished. Sit down.

712
00:53:10,854 --> 00:53:11,888
Board chairman.

713
00:53:15,926 --> 00:53:18,762
I am holding you accountable
for the loss of our doctors.

714
00:53:21,798 --> 00:53:23,166
Shigekatsu Hiruma,

715
00:53:23,867 --> 00:53:25,802
I hereby announce your transfer
to the 16th branch clinic.

716
00:53:27,170 --> 00:53:28,171
What?

717
00:53:36,246 --> 00:53:37,514
Minami.

718
00:53:39,549 --> 00:53:43,053
- I will move to Shanghai as well.
- Huh?

719
00:53:43,453 --> 00:53:44,588
I'll be in charge of PR.

720
00:53:48,758 --> 00:53:50,493
- Good luck.
- Huh?

721
00:53:53,530 --> 00:53:54,631
- Good luck.
- Good luck.

722
00:53:58,835 --> 00:54:00,937
Happy new year.

723
00:54:04,007 --> 00:54:07,043
Thank you for
using Michiko Daimon and...

724
00:54:07,177 --> 00:54:09,713
Hiromi Jonouchi
for the past three months.

725
00:54:13,316 --> 00:54:14,884
- Here are two melons.
- Huh?

726
00:54:18,088 --> 00:54:20,323
The bill from last year.

727
00:54:21,725 --> 00:54:22,559
Well...

728
00:54:23,360 --> 00:54:29,165
he just became an ex-hospital director,
so please give it to the new one.

729
00:54:29,299 --> 00:54:34,104
No. You're in charge of the bill
for the last year.

730
00:54:39,442 --> 00:54:41,311
The contract is terminated.

731
00:54:44,481 --> 00:54:47,651
Hail to Toutei University Hospital!

732
00:54:52,088 --> 00:54:55,125
What do you plan to do, Rika?

733
00:55:01,564 --> 00:55:03,933
Hey!

734
00:55:11,708 --> 00:55:18,148
I'll move... to the 16th branch.

735
00:55:18,982 --> 00:55:24,587
Will you two be coming with me?
I didn't think you would.

736
00:55:37,200 --> 00:55:40,303
The one and only

737
00:55:40,804 --> 00:55:44,941
- Mum, I'll write you from London again.
- Okay.

738
00:55:46,176 --> 00:55:51,514
To be honest, I gave up once.
I thought I'd never see you again.

739
00:55:52,415 --> 00:55:53,350
Mum.

740
00:55:54,117 --> 00:55:57,821
But Dr. Daimon...
never gave up, even once.

741
00:55:59,022 --> 00:56:02,225
So, Mai, I want you to believe
in your own strength as well.

742
00:56:03,960 --> 00:56:08,798
Mai, miracles might not
be the work of god,

743
00:56:09,199 --> 00:56:11,568
but of people.

744
00:56:13,870 --> 00:56:15,839
I wonder if there are any
good men in London.

745
00:56:15,905 --> 00:56:17,907
- Michael!
- Michael?

746
00:56:17,974 --> 00:56:19,642
- How old he is?
- He's 10 years old.

747
00:56:19,709 --> 00:56:21,077
10 years old?

748
00:56:28,952 --> 00:56:32,055
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

749
00:56:49,706 --> 00:56:51,708
Where did Michiko go?

750
00:56:52,842 --> 00:56:54,677
Space? New York?

751
00:56:55,612 --> 00:56:57,781
Maybe even a deserted island.

752
00:56:59,015 --> 00:57:01,084
Right? Ben Casey.

753
00:57:10,126 --> 00:57:12,729
I slept like a log!

754
00:57:15,532 --> 00:57:16,633
You scared me!

755
00:57:17,600 --> 00:57:19,569
Mr. Akira, I'm hungry.

756
00:57:19,636 --> 00:57:21,104
Where were you?

757
00:57:21,538 --> 00:57:23,473
How could you sleep that long?

758
00:57:23,540 --> 00:57:25,508
- That was too long!
- My body aches.

759
00:57:25,575 --> 00:57:27,277
Ouch, my shoulders.

760
00:57:28,778 --> 00:57:31,648
Hello.
You have a frozen food delivered.

761
00:57:31,714 --> 00:57:32,849
Here you are.

762
00:57:33,049 --> 00:57:34,951
Here you are.

763
00:57:35,018 --> 00:57:36,119
What is it?

764
00:57:37,153 --> 00:57:39,656
Toko Kubo from Shanghai.
Frozen gyoza!

765
00:57:39,722 --> 00:57:41,391
Yes!

766
00:57:41,458 --> 00:57:43,626
Please sign here.

767
00:57:43,693 --> 00:57:45,094
- Do you have a pen?
- Pen?

768
00:57:47,163 --> 00:57:49,332
I have a pen.

769
00:57:53,870 --> 00:57:54,871
Oh, what's wrong?

770
00:58:02,078 --> 00:58:03,513
Mr. Akira, call an ambulance.

771
00:58:03,580 --> 00:58:05,281
- It seems like myocardial infarction.
- Got it.

772
00:58:06,249 --> 00:58:08,251
Am I going to die?

773
00:58:08,685 --> 00:58:09,919
No, I won't let you.

774
00:58:12,755 --> 00:58:14,190
- Here you go, Michiko.
- Oh, thanks.

775
00:58:15,258 --> 00:58:16,125
Thank you.

776
00:58:17,393 --> 00:58:19,262
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

777
00:58:19,996 --> 00:58:22,866
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>

778
00:58:23,366 --> 00:58:24,501
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

779
00:58:25,468 --> 00:58:28,438
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>

780
00:58:29,038 --> 00:58:30,507
<i>and the skills she has earned.</i>

781
00:58:35,512 --> 00:58:37,680
I never fail.

782
00:58:40,216 --> 00:58:42,285
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

783
00:58:43,019 --> 00:58:43,953
<i>Also known as</i>

784
00:58:44,521 --> 00:58:45,955
<i>Doctor-X.</i>
